From: Kostiantyn Andriiuk <konstantin@andriyuk.com>
Subject: [PATCH] GLFW: map Wayland touch to pointer input for SDR++

Handle touch down, motion, release and cancellation, including all optional
listener callbacks. Name the private library libglfw-vince so the system
GLFW library remains unchanged. This is a locally modified GLFW 3.4.

Base: https://github.com/glfw/glfw/tree/3.4
SPDX-License-Identifier: Zlib

diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@ endif()
-
+
 if (UNIX AND GLFW_BUILD_SHARED_LIBRARY)
     # On Unix-like systems, shared libraries can use the soname system.
-    set(GLFW_LIB_NAME glfw)
+    set(GLFW_LIB_NAME glfw-vince)
 else()
     set(GLFW_LIB_NAME glfw3)
 endif()
